WEBVTT

00:04.630 --> 00:06.710
Don't let it bother you, Lulu.

00:06.710 --> 00:08.710
I doubt anyone died.

00:08.710 --> 00:11.940
Your pleading with the elemental paid off.

00:12.890 --> 00:13.700
But...

00:14.490 --> 00:19.240
No innocents got involved and the
 security cameras were destroyed.

00:19.240 --> 00:22.060
The elders don't take chances 
with that sort of thing.

00:22.060 --> 00:25.310
I knew our group wasn't all one happy family,

00:25.310 --> 00:29.500
but where do they get off,
 trying to shut us down so openly?

00:30.710 --> 00:33.670
<b>Fire 
Safety</b>

00:31.130 --> 00:33.180
They're afraid of the Bug.

00:33.920 --> 00:38.280
They fled this country and built 
a remote base in Eastern Europe,

00:38.280 --> 00:42.890
so they don't want me leaking information 
that could get them burned, too.

00:43.450 --> 00:47.210
I do have a stake in this, though, 
so I think I'll burn before I get burned.

00:47.210 --> 00:48.020
Huh?

00:48.340 --> 00:53.050
There's a Japanese saying: 
"summer bugs fly to flame."

00:53.050 --> 00:56.490
And I'd say I'm the best 
bait to draw out this bug.

00:57.370 --> 01:01.220
I'll advertise my presence and 
gather them all in this city.

01:01.730 --> 01:04.860
Doesn't crushing them in one fell 
swoop sound like a plan to you?

02:39.090 --> 02:41.790
Can I ask you something?

02:41.790 --> 02:43.090
Yes?

02:43.090 --> 02:46.390
Why did you visit that 
fortune teller's building?

02:47.170 --> 02:50.440
Was that giant swarm of hands 
one of your magic tricks?

02:51.240 --> 02:53.400
Why do you want to know?

02:53.840 --> 02:58.090
Because you may have 
already reached your goal.

02:58.550 --> 03:02.470
The thing my employers spent 
a century searching for.

03:02.470 --> 03:04.370
You have my attention.

03:04.970 --> 03:10.000
You're already involved. 
In fact, this all revolves around you.

03:10.310 --> 03:15.760
You may lose your own head 
instead of a dummy's next time.

03:19.600 --> 03:21.550
N-No! I can't take it!

03:22.260 --> 03:23.270
Shut up.

03:23.270 --> 03:24.610
Sorry, sorry.

03:24.610 --> 03:27.140
It's just too, too much!

03:28.190 --> 03:32.460
I feel so sorry for the guy,
 I might let him ditching me slide.

03:32.460 --> 03:34.590
Still, I envy Higuro-san.

03:34.590 --> 03:37.390
This means he made friends 
with Solitaire, right?

03:37.390 --> 03:39.110
Do you think he could get me an autograph?

03:40.090 --> 03:45.070
If only Majiri-neesan could get 
along with those kids this well.

03:46.250 --> 03:48.540
That must be the building.

03:49.250 --> 03:52.170
I wonder if the little assassin is in.

03:53.450 --> 03:55.250
Do you know?

03:58.410 --> 04:01.130
Heilei, I presume?

04:01.660 --> 04:05.450
Wonderful. I've been hoping 
to pay my respects.

04:05.840 --> 04:10.040
You see, that boy, Xiaoyu-kun, 
is going to be my little brother.

04:10.040 --> 04:13.600
So we'll be relatives from now on.

04:13.600 --> 04:14.650
<b>Found found found found found found found 
found Agakura Agakura Agakura Agakura
 Agakura Agakura thief thief thief</b>

04:16.860 --> 04:19.290
Mind your manners.

04:19.290 --> 04:20.940
Calling for backup won't—

04:25.070 --> 04:27.160
m 0 0 l 300 0 300 150 0 150

04:25.070 --> 04:27.160
<b>This evil, vile, despicable fiend took your 
arms and legs and pride, my dear, precious 
darling, and now she's trying to take you
 from me. Don't worry. I'll kill kill kill kill 
KILL kill kill kill kill kill kill her, so you 
can relax. Big Sis will get back absolutely 
everything—your limbs and your heart. I'll 
get it all back, so...</b>

04:25.550 --> 04:26.780
A word of warning.

04:27.570 --> 04:29.870
I see. You're...

04:29.870 --> 04:34.870
Heilei Officer: Bao

04:29.870 --> 04:34.870
<b>Real Name: Yanmei Lei</b>

04:30.120 --> 04:33.900
I'm the only big sister Xiaoyu needs.

04:35.930 --> 04:41.090
The Heilei don't need an incompetent 
who lost to an Agakura girl!

04:41.090 --> 04:43.960
I'll dispose of him myself if you—

04:47.850 --> 04:50.640
How fierce, even for a daughter of mine.

04:52.850 --> 04:59.820
She even tried to kill <i>me</i> when I 
announced I'd make Xiaoyu a ting-hu.

05:00.090 --> 05:03.900
Don't insult Xiaoyu—my brother.

05:06.410 --> 05:11.050
So, you want revenge for 
the dear little assassin?

05:11.400 --> 05:12.810
Not quite.

05:12.810 --> 05:14.330
No?

05:14.630 --> 05:17.000
You're right that Xiaoyu is a dear.

05:17.000 --> 05:19.290
Yes! Isn't he just?!

05:21.040 --> 05:25.600
I hate you for hurting my brother, 
but I'm also grateful.

05:26.680 --> 05:28.750
Grateful? Really?

05:28.750 --> 05:33.540
Losing his limbs is what let 
him escape our cursed family.

05:34.030 --> 05:35.310
I'm surprised.

05:39.610 --> 05:44.490
I thought the Heilei obsessed 
over their lineage.

05:45.950 --> 05:48.520
I'm not interested in old-fashioned values,

05:48.520 --> 05:54.030
but if you intend to take 
my brother from me, then die.

05:55.600 --> 05:58.580
Can you really make magic from this?

05:58.580 --> 06:02.350
Yes. It should let us recharge your arm, too.

06:02.350 --> 06:04.500
Jewels as fuel?

06:04.500 --> 06:07.860
No wonder Miss Sayo wanted 
all those junk stones.

06:08.340 --> 06:11.680
If raw stones work, you can 
buy them cheaper and in bulk.

06:11.910 --> 06:17.100
Clearer and larger stones contain more mana.

06:17.810 --> 06:20.150
Then there's the problem of money.

06:20.530 --> 06:25.560
I'd like to gather resources to 
recover the real Polka-kun,

06:25.990 --> 06:29.360
but I can't exactly ask Rozan-san for help.

06:30.910 --> 06:32.600
It's my fault.

06:33.480 --> 06:38.960
I'm the only guard who knew 
that plushie is the real Polka.

06:38.960 --> 06:40.670
That's not true.

06:40.950 --> 06:44.710
But anyway, we'd better 
report this to Rozan-san.

06:44.920 --> 06:46.630
His Lordship?

06:46.630 --> 06:48.150
No can do.

06:48.150 --> 06:48.840
What?

06:48.840 --> 06:52.020
Grandfather should be in the hospital today.

06:52.020 --> 06:53.760
Oh, right. Today is...

06:53.760 --> 06:55.740
His regular check-up.

06:55.740 --> 06:59.140
He's probably fully anesthetized 
and in no shape to talk.

06:59.670 --> 07:02.840
<i>I felt a moment of relief just then.</i>

07:04.030 --> 07:06.810
<i>I almost thought that I could rescue Polka</i>

07:06.810 --> 07:10.200
<i>and fix my mistake before 
His Lordship found out.</i>

07:11.140 --> 07:12.870
I'm the worst.

07:13.410 --> 07:17.580
Because you were halfhearted about 
protecting the real Polka-kun?

07:18.820 --> 07:19.710
That's none of—

07:19.710 --> 07:23.020
—my business? Are you sure, 
with the way things are going?

07:24.090 --> 07:27.400
You don't have to rush, but you can talk to me.

07:30.140 --> 07:33.460
Something about him... 
always got on my nerves.

07:34.280 --> 07:39.480
But I didn't really hate 
him until just recently.

07:40.090 --> 07:42.770
He acts without any regard for 
His Lordship's feelings.

07:43.670 --> 07:47.500
I take pride in these limbs 
that Rozan-sama gave me.

07:48.080 --> 07:51.670
But he's Rozan-sama's own son.

07:51.670 --> 07:57.240
Doesn't his body, his blood 
ties, mean anything to him?

07:57.850 --> 08:01.470
I can never have those ties, 
no matter how hard I try.

08:01.970 --> 08:04.460
I can't become Rozan-sama's real son.

08:04.830 --> 08:09.490
But... he acts like it's nothing to him.

08:09.920 --> 08:12.140
No. I'm making excuses.

08:12.140 --> 08:15.390
I just envied him. Forget it.

08:20.750 --> 08:22.370
How pathetic.

08:24.760 --> 08:28.850
My father... sold me for money.

08:29.780 --> 08:33.780
He ended up stabbing me to 
death to satisfy his own greed.

08:36.240 --> 08:39.900
So I envy bonds with blood family, too,

08:40.750 --> 08:45.710
but I can tell you feel just as 
strong a bond with Rozan-san.

08:49.170 --> 08:52.670
I'm sure that's not one-sided.

08:53.290 --> 08:57.390
You may not share blood
but your souls are linked,

08:58.950 --> 09:03.720
so you should treasure that tie, too.

09:05.180 --> 09:08.770
Losing either kind of connection
 will hurt just as much.

09:11.430 --> 09:13.370
So this time,

09:14.530 --> 09:17.280
I <i>will</i> make a world where 
we can all live in peace.

09:21.790 --> 09:22.860
Hello.

09:22.860 --> 09:27.060
What is it, Nezu? Have you finished work?

09:29.190 --> 09:31.630
You'll rejoin us in three days?

09:31.630 --> 09:37.010
<b>Lunch Meeting
 
Management Strategy
 Session 

Corporate Planning 
Committee 
 
Management Meeting 

 Private Event</b>

09:31.630 --> 09:37.010
m 0 0 l 120 0 120 130 0 130

09:32.150 --> 09:35.470
Perfect. I have a job for you.

09:37.530 --> 09:43.140
<b>Two Days To Go</b>

09:38.490 --> 09:40.530
Well, that about sums it up.

09:40.530 --> 09:43.140
I'm sorry for asking so much of you.

09:43.620 --> 09:45.780
Don't sweat it.

09:45.780 --> 09:49.670
Supporting your peaceful 
life is what I'm here for.

09:49.670 --> 09:52.560
Polka-kun's kidnapping 
yesterday was hardly peaceful,

09:52.560 --> 09:55.510
and neither is the rest of 
what I've dragged you into.

09:55.510 --> 09:57.610
All for a peaceful future, though, right?

09:59.540 --> 10:01.030
But anyway,

10:01.030 --> 10:06.500
<b><b>Strange happenings beset city! 
 A challenge from Solitaire?! 

</b>Witnesses report a range of bizarre phenomena!<b></b></b>

10:01.030 --> 10:06.500
<b>m 0 0 l 600 0 600 120 0 120</b>

10:01.350 --> 10:04.550
this dude seriously never quits.

10:04.550 --> 10:06.500
What is he thinking?

10:07.760 --> 10:08.580
Huh?

10:13.570 --> 10:14.960
What's that?

10:16.940 --> 10:17.920
<b>Solitaire has arrived</b>

10:18.770 --> 10:20.430
What is he after?

10:20.430 --> 10:23.390
Asking why he does anything 
is a waste of time.

10:23.390 --> 10:28.850
<b>Strange happenings beset city! 
A challenge from Solitaire?! 
Witnesses report a range of bizarre phenomena!</b>

10:23.710 --> 10:28.850
But the inspector is currently attached 
to HQ's Solitaire task force.

10:29.480 --> 10:34.690
Surely we need to at least look 
like we're prioritizing that case.

10:34.690 --> 10:36.240
Ugh.

10:36.240 --> 10:37.090
No.

10:37.090 --> 10:39.660
That jackass Solitaire didn't do this.

10:40.090 --> 10:41.740
A copycat?

10:41.970 --> 10:43.930
I'm only going on a hunch,

10:43.930 --> 10:48.790
but just lifting something and dropping 
it is nothing new for stage magic.

10:48.790 --> 10:52.750
Solitaire usually makes his 
tricks significant in some way.

10:53.510 --> 10:57.680
Which begs the question of who's behind this.

10:57.680 --> 11:01.080
Another troublemaker, like Deus Ex Kinema?

11:01.080 --> 11:02.330
Or...

11:02.960 --> 11:03.750
Never mind.

11:04.810 --> 11:08.480
Either way, we can't stand 
around twiddling our thumbs.

11:08.970 --> 11:12.430
Damn it. We've got all 
these cases in Shinjuku.

11:12.430 --> 11:15.440
What connects them all, and how deeply?

11:16.240 --> 11:20.280
Good grief. A copycat of <i>me</i>?

11:20.280 --> 11:22.730
I know just who would pull a stunt like this.

11:22.730 --> 11:25.950
To me, hunting this organization 
is an adventure.

11:25.950 --> 11:29.910
But to you, I see, it's fodder 
for a documentary film!

11:30.130 --> 11:34.630
Isn't it, troublemaker emperor of Ikebukuro, 
Deus Ex Kinema-kun?!

11:35.510 --> 11:36.950
U-Um...

11:37.590 --> 11:39.320
I'm so, so sorry.

11:39.320 --> 11:40.630
You have the wrong person.

11:40.630 --> 11:41.970
<i>Who's she?!</i>

11:42.320 --> 11:44.810
Pleased to meet you. I'm a fan.

11:44.810 --> 11:49.640
I see. I suppose I should be relieved 
that this wasn't a police trap?

11:49.980 --> 11:52.350
That depends on your attitude.

11:52.800 --> 11:55.810
Meaning you're scarier than the police?

11:55.810 --> 11:59.530
Unfortunately, my homeland 
doesn't use business cards.

12:00.220 --> 12:04.010
Will this serve to identify us instead?

12:04.660 --> 12:06.770
The Byadian Imperial Crest.

12:06.770 --> 12:10.950
That's the proper name of the 
emblem you've been broadcasting.

12:13.520 --> 12:16.130
It's hopeless. This will take too long.

12:16.510 --> 12:19.590
But... considering the risks, 
I can't settle for less.

12:19.840 --> 12:24.090
Hey, is it true you you called 
up one of your friends' ghosts?

12:24.090 --> 12:27.550
I didn't call him so much 
as he showed up uninvited.

12:27.900 --> 12:30.580
So you <i>did</i> have friends in your world!

12:32.180 --> 12:35.230
I treasure you and Takumi-kun 
as friends, too.

12:35.230 --> 12:38.160
Hmm... You've said that before,

12:38.160 --> 12:40.230
but we only just met, you know?

12:40.580 --> 12:46.160
My teacher told me that,
 to long-lived necromancers like us,

12:46.160 --> 12:49.200
bonds with people can't be 
measured in time spent together.

12:49.770 --> 12:53.180
Did you make friends with your 
buddy from back home this quickly?

12:53.180 --> 12:54.490
Let me think.

12:54.490 --> 12:58.050
He came on so strong that I didn't 
know what to do a lot of the time,

12:58.050 --> 13:01.880
but he's my dear friend... and my accomplice.

13:01.880 --> 13:02.880
Why accomplice?

13:03.320 --> 13:06.050
Sorry. Maybe I worded that wrong.

13:06.050 --> 13:08.810
We got up to a lot of mischief together.

13:08.810 --> 13:10.480
Hmm?

13:10.480 --> 13:13.340
Those three who abducted the real Polka-kun

13:13.870 --> 13:19.040
have some kind of powerful ties to 
the other world, too. I'm sure of it.

13:19.630 --> 13:22.330
I don't know if we're 
caught in their business,

13:22.330 --> 13:24.970
or if I dragged them into ours, but—

13:26.070 --> 13:29.830
I got you and the other Polka-kun 
involved in the first place.

13:29.830 --> 13:33.370
I slit Polka-kun's throat,

13:33.370 --> 13:38.790
then I tried to kill you again when you 
came back, dragging you into my world.

13:38.790 --> 13:40.700
That'sh naht weally—

13:40.700 --> 13:45.760
Everyone, good or bad,
 drags others into their lives sometimes.

13:46.130 --> 13:52.100
So when it comes down to it, just drag 
everyone into what you think is best.

13:53.690 --> 13:57.080
I <i>want</i> to get mixed up 
in your business, anyway.

13:57.640 --> 14:00.840
Let's go save the real Polka-kun together.

14:02.090 --> 14:03.230
Thank you.

14:04.660 --> 14:06.030
I see.

14:06.030 --> 14:10.990
You want to advertise your 
relation to this "Sabaramond."

14:11.200 --> 14:13.090
Yes, I suppose so.

14:13.090 --> 14:16.750
I don't care how. 
We could even be guests on your show.

14:16.750 --> 14:19.040
Yay!

14:17.250 --> 14:19.040
The three of us could dance, if you like.

14:19.040 --> 14:19.750
Huh?!

14:20.030 --> 14:24.960
Suspected space aliens dancing? 
You have my attention.

14:24.960 --> 14:26.620
Aliens?

14:26.620 --> 14:31.840
That aside, I thought you were 
seeking supernatural phenomena.

14:31.840 --> 14:34.510
Doesn't this situation excite you?

14:34.510 --> 14:38.630
Not really? Secretly, my heart 
is swelling with anticipation,

14:38.630 --> 14:40.480
but I can't make up my mind.

14:40.780 --> 14:41.810
About what?

14:42.040 --> 14:43.770
A feat like yours

14:45.610 --> 14:49.400
is easy enough to replicate with tricks.

14:49.400 --> 14:50.450
Oh?

14:50.450 --> 14:51.840
Wait. Seriously?

14:51.840 --> 14:54.200
Does he have a great spirit, too?!

14:55.570 --> 14:56.790
So this

14:56.790 --> 14:59.870
is where that fire broke out 100 years ago.

15:00.260 --> 15:04.340
Now, does anything here connect 
to the Fire-Breathing Bug?

15:04.760 --> 15:07.530
They've prettied up the exterior,

15:07.530 --> 15:08.920
but something's off.

15:09.340 --> 15:12.850
A wealthy Shinjuku dynasty owns this place,

15:13.210 --> 15:16.810
and apparently they paid a 
fortune for it after the fire.

15:17.310 --> 15:22.690
Their descendants live elsewhere, 
but they've never tried to sell the place.

15:22.690 --> 15:27.500
But are you sure we should be here? 
It has nothing to do with Solitaire.

15:27.920 --> 15:32.660
No, they've been too 
close lately to say that.

15:33.510 --> 15:38.390
At heart, every troublemaker 
only follows their own goals.

15:38.700 --> 15:42.610
Except for the Grocer, none of them 
would ever seek each other out.

15:43.210 --> 15:47.090
But between this "Sabaramond" 
group and that symbol,

15:47.890 --> 15:50.190
this pair's interests overlap too much.

15:50.550 --> 15:54.140
You mean Solitaire and the Fire-Breathing 
Bug have already joined forces?

15:54.380 --> 15:57.770
Yeah, probably. And in earnest.

15:59.300 --> 16:03.020
As for your request, I'd be delighted.

16:03.020 --> 16:05.110
But on one condition.

16:05.390 --> 16:08.070
That sounds like fun. What condition?

16:08.360 --> 16:11.210
Well, I insist

16:12.070 --> 16:15.260
that you somehow manage to survive.

16:17.710 --> 16:31.920
Never shall we forget the days we've shared,

16:31.920 --> 16:47.440
yet 'tis time we go our 
separate ways. Goodbye.

16:33.530 --> 16:36.130
I didn't expect to see you so soon!

16:40.740 --> 16:48.150
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

16:48.940 --> 16:49.740
Whoa!

16:49.740 --> 16:50.900
Civil-sama!

16:50.900 --> 16:55.950
Oh, so you burst liquid fuel 
in midair and set fire to it.

16:56.270 --> 16:59.080
<i>I hope that's not a mix of 
naphthetic and palmitic acids,</i>

16:59.080 --> 17:03.760
<i>i.e., the fuel for napalm 
bombs and flamethrowers.</i>

17:03.760 --> 17:06.790
<i>Because if it is, the extreme 
heat will roast me, too.</i>

17:06.790 --> 17:08.540
<i>It's not, right? Please say it's not.</i>

17:08.540 --> 17:12.280
<i>I believe you have at least some morals,
 Fire-Breathing Bug-kun.</i>

17:12.280 --> 17:13.970
<i>Oh, I have a bad feeling about this!</i>

17:16.720 --> 17:17.840
Perfect timing.

17:17.840 --> 17:19.820
I've been hoping to test this out.

17:20.430 --> 17:23.060
Maybe something like... this?

17:24.310 --> 17:26.350
Whoa. You've gotta be kidding me.

17:27.770 --> 17:30.480
Hmm... Was that right?

17:30.890 --> 17:34.900
No, I suppose I need to 
follow the proper steps.

17:41.970 --> 17:43.640
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

17:41.970 --> 17:44.910
I sympathize with you Bugs!

17:45.140 --> 17:48.210
I can guess what you really are!

17:50.030 --> 17:53.320
In this country, 100 years ago, my affiliates

17:53.320 --> 17:55.880
performed experiments to 
give humans special powers!

17:56.360 --> 17:57.470
<b>PEEK<b></b></b>

17:56.360 --> 17:57.470
PEEK<b></b>

17:57.470 --> 18:02.560
To maintain secrecy, they supposedly 
incinerated all 18 test subjects.

17:57.470 --> 18:02.560
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

18:02.770 --> 18:04.930
But only 16 bodies were found.

18:04.930 --> 18:06.520
I take it some survived?

18:07.560 --> 18:09.450
And they multiplied

18:09.450 --> 18:12.280
to enact their vengeance on us.

18:11.900 --> 18:22.370
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

18:12.730 --> 18:15.840
I don't know how you did it, 
whether by science or magic,

18:15.840 --> 18:22.370
but you implanted a lust for revenge 
in others—ordinary, innocent people.

18:22.630 --> 18:24.720
I admire your tenacity.

18:24.720 --> 18:26.660
That said,

18:27.090 --> 18:32.880
aren't you doing just what our elders 
did to the 18 whose lives they took?

18:33.290 --> 18:36.210
In terms of sheer numbers,
 you're even worse than they were.

18:36.470 --> 18:38.720
Exactly.

18:38.720 --> 18:54.690
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

18:38.950 --> 18:41.920
Therefore, we, too, are evil.

18:41.920 --> 18:45.930
Merely bugs seared into this world.

18:46.370 --> 18:49.650
Once we have burned you all,

18:49.960 --> 18:53.550
we shall vanish from within these people.

18:53.550 --> 18:54.690
Shall burn away.

18:54.690 --> 18:59.530
Good. If you feel that way, 
then I feel no personal guilt.

18:59.530 --> 19:02.490
Now, let's slug it out!

19:02.490 --> 19:04.490
Put our existences on the line!

19:05.060 --> 19:07.080
A childish taunt.

19:08.930 --> 19:11.120
A smoke screen? It won't work.

19:16.020 --> 19:18.050
A mass disappearing act?!

19:18.470 --> 19:20.630
Huh?! Did they run out on us?!

19:21.070 --> 19:22.410
I see.

19:22.740 --> 19:25.350
It seems revenge hasn't 
given them tunnel vision.

19:26.120 --> 19:30.190
I suppose they were evaluating 
our combat strength just now.

19:30.510 --> 19:35.080
Far better than a "summer bug" who 
flies into flames without thinking.

19:34.830 --> 19:36.090
SHOCK

19:34.830 --> 19:36.090
SHOCK

19:35.080 --> 19:36.190
Shock.

19:36.680 --> 19:41.370
Think this guy knows where they hide out?

19:42.300 --> 19:45.030
Mademoiselle, even if I did know,

19:45.030 --> 19:47.580
do I look like I would 
sell out a friend so easily?!

19:47.580 --> 19:48.640
Yeah.

19:48.640 --> 19:49.470
I'd say so.

19:49.470 --> 19:50.370
Yes.

19:50.370 --> 19:51.730
Well, don't be hasty.

19:51.730 --> 19:55.130
Allow me to tell you a choice secret instead.

19:55.130 --> 19:56.030
Like what?

19:56.030 --> 19:57.800
The saying "summer bugs fly to flame"

19:57.800 --> 19:59.820
originates in the Chinese <i>Book 
of Liang</i>'s "Life of Dao Gai."

19:59.820 --> 20:01.520
And it's not about tactics or traps.

20:01.520 --> 20:03.590
You see, an old man jealous of 
his more talented grandson—

20:01.520 --> 20:03.590
Who cares?!

20:03.590 --> 20:08.560
As interesting as that sounds, 
I have a different question for you.

20:09.320 --> 20:11.640
After you obtained the emblem,

20:11.640 --> 20:14.380
why did you visit that building in Shinjuku?

20:14.380 --> 20:17.360
Does it have anything to do with the 
young fortune teller who lives there?

20:18.580 --> 20:21.820
Are you certain you don't 
have your answer already?

20:23.020 --> 20:26.440
A bug flying to a flame may be foolish,

20:26.440 --> 20:30.160
but what if that bug 
could withstand the heat?

20:30.660 --> 20:31.370
You—

20:31.370 --> 20:33.500
Better luck
 next time

20:32.490 --> 20:33.500
Huh?

20:33.500 --> 20:34.960
And...

20:34.960 --> 20:38.920
leaping into fire is the only way to 
see some worlds. Wouldn't you agree?

20:39.160 --> 20:41.350
While your powers do interest me,

20:41.350 --> 20:43.840
I have a busy night ahead.

20:44.540 --> 20:48.560
Bewitch me with a world free of 
tricks and illusions someday!

20:48.560 --> 20:50.170
For that,

20:50.170 --> 20:53.600
I'll enter the fire as 
many times as it takes.

20:56.850 --> 20:59.690
I knew visiting this country was a good idea.

21:00.410 --> 21:04.820
It's done a little to quench the 
thirst I've felt since I was born.

21:04.820 --> 21:07.570
I don't get any of this!

21:07.570 --> 21:11.610
Hey, Boss! What was that big-ass 
wind-cannon thing, anyway?!

21:11.610 --> 21:15.120
It wasn't like the great 
spirit's power, was it?

21:15.120 --> 21:17.660
Oh, that. I tried it, and it worked.

21:17.660 --> 21:19.590
You can just <i>do</i> that?

21:20.360 --> 21:25.570
Until now, I've only been able to use 
magic to enhance my flesh and nerves.

21:25.940 --> 21:28.010
I am a failure, after all.

21:28.760 --> 21:33.220
Didn't I tell you before we came here?
 About my absurd origins.

21:33.820 --> 21:39.430
My body was meant for the copied mind 
and memory of a sorcerer from the other side.

21:39.910 --> 21:42.790
His name was Arius Sabaramond.

21:43.450 --> 21:48.450
But in the end, that "great sorcerer" 
never appeared in this world.

21:48.710 --> 21:52.950
And yet the organization 
continues to cling to his name.

21:52.950 --> 21:57.290
"The Bastard Children of 
Sabaramond." Oh, the irony.

21:57.770 --> 22:02.350
I was a failure, unable to so 
much as cast a spell, until—

22:02.350 --> 22:05.010
Yes, that was the trigger.

22:05.210 --> 22:09.300
I'd never felt my mana tampered 
with from the outside before.

22:09.880 --> 22:14.190
I wondered if I could do it in 
reverse, and lucky for us, it worked.

22:14.190 --> 22:16.490
There he goes, bragging about his talent.

22:16.490 --> 22:18.520
Amazing, Civil-sama!

22:18.880 --> 22:21.320
Well, I'm just starting out.

22:21.320 --> 22:23.780
Once I get the hang of it, I can—

22:24.230 --> 22:26.980
Oh, I like you, Soara, Lulu.

22:27.300 --> 22:29.780
You help me feel the other world.

22:29.780 --> 22:32.300
Warn me before you say crap like that.

22:33.580 --> 22:38.730
But <i>this</i> world isn't lawless 
enough for me to act freely.

22:39.230 --> 22:44.000
I've always felt that this 
world isn't where I belong.

22:44.570 --> 22:48.970
I was made on the other side,
 so I want to go back.

22:48.970 --> 22:51.970
Back to the precious 
homeland I've never seen.

22:53.760 --> 22:56.840
If I can't return, then I hope

22:56.840 --> 23:01.400
this world can at least offer 
something to cure my boredom.

23:04.820 --> 23:07.720
Hello. I'm impressed you found this number.

23:07.720 --> 23:11.200
We've never spoken directly before. 
Are introductions in order?

23:11.200 --> 23:16.020
Oh, no. Not at all, Sabaramond-sama.

23:16.020 --> 23:20.160
You've been patronizing our 
store since before we relocated.

23:20.570 --> 23:25.130
Since you called, I assume 
you've stocked my order?

23:25.860 --> 23:27.970
Information about Polka Shinoyama's family,

23:27.970 --> 23:33.550
and especially his mother, Kanon Shinoyama?
